+# Prospective config-v2 sidecar
+
+This optional producer hook records the exact public run stratum before the solver starts. It does
+not read archives, journals, grades, outcomes, predictions, or environment dumps, and it does not
+change the task, solver, operator, model, or budget.
+
+## Enable for a new prospective batch
+
+Set both variables in the launch environment before starting the run:
+
+```bash
+export DOJO_CONFIG_V2_SIDECAR=1
+export DOJO_GENERATOR_RELEASE=<public-release-label-or-unknown>
+```
+
+`HARDWARE` is populated by `dojo.main_run` before the hook executes. The hook is disabled when
+`DOJO_CONFIG_V2_SIDECAR` is absent or `0`; every other value except `1` is rejected to catch typos.
+When enabled, a missing release or hardware label fails before task construction and solver
+execution. Literal `unknown` is allowed for honest provenance, but downstream exact-stratum
+interaction gates must treat it as incomplete metadata.
+
+Each run writes `producer.config_v2.jsonl` under its output directory after `dojo_config.json` is
+saved and before `env_variables.json` or any solver outcome is produced. The file contains one
+canonical JSON row with public fields and SHA-256 fingerprints only. The resolved solver projection
+itself is never written. Existing output is never overwritten; checkpoint/resume may reuse an
+existing sidecar only when its bytes are exactly identical to the newly computed bytes.
+
+## Merge an archive batch
+
+Pass every per-run sidecar explicitly; the collector does not scan directories:
+
+```bash
+python -m dojo.utils.config_v2_sidecar \
+  --sidecar <run-1>/producer.config_v2.jsonl \
+  --sidecar <run-2>/producer.config_v2.jsonl \
+  --output <archive-basename>.config_v2.jsonl
+```
+
+The collector verifies the exact ten-field schema and both hashes, rejects credentials, symlinks,
+noncanonical bytes and duplicate physical run IDs, sorts bytewise by run ID, then publishes through
+a no-clobber atomic hard link. It does not infer missing runs or metadata and never opens an archive.
+Upload the immutable batch sidecar beside the corresponding archive before outcome analysis.
